Hi to everyone,
today i decided to get back to my VAX 11/725.
The machine seems to be in good conditions except for the tu58 drive, which
suffer from the capstan problem, and completely ruined the firmware tape
(this happened before i got my hands on the machine :-( ).
I think i found the tape images for the firmware, now all i need is to
setup a machine with dos/unix to run the emulator and connect the
vax to the "fake" drive.

I wasn't able to found an explicit scheme for the tu58--pc_serial cable
i need to build, so after some research i came up with this:

     TU58 DRIVE CONNECTOR

     (male)     (female)
    ___---___   ___---___
   |0 2 4 6 8| |8 6 4 2 0|
   |1 3 X 7 9| |9 7 X 3 1|
    ---------   ---------

   0 --> GND
   1 --> AUX-B
   2 --> RX-
   3 --> RX+
   4 --> GND
   5 --> *NOT CONNECTED*
   6 --> TX+
   7 --> TX-
   8 --> AUX-A
   9 --> GND


  Connection to RS232 (crossed)
  
  TU58  ----  DB9
    3 -------> 3 (tx)
    6 -------> 2 (rx)
    2 --,----> 5 (gnd)
    7 __|

Would this work? do i need to gnd the AUX signals? anyone attempted to
do this?

Any help would be greatly appreciated!!
Hkz

