Uhmm... i had a second tought on this one...
as the pinout TU58 i have found is for the DRIVE, and not the controller,
i think that this would be more correct:

  TU58  ----  DB9
    3 -------> 2 (rx)
    6 -------> 3 (tx)
    2 --,----> 5 (gnd)
    7 __|

This is because if the pin is named RX on the drive, the pc emulating it
should also receive on it, same consideration for the TX.

