Hi,
those who read my previous post might have guessed that i'm trying to
resurrect an old VAX 11/725: that's right, but this dinosaur is giving
me a lot of problems :)
First i had problems with the dead power supply (caused by some
"rotten" capacitors), then with the melted capstans in the TU58 drive
(problem solved by using an emulator), now i've got problems with the CPU.

I had success loading the console tape, but the diagnostics give me
a lot of trouble: as soon as the software starts, it halt itself
on the CPU test giving a "BAD CPU" error, and telling me to phone
the assistance service (hehe, i could try to phone HP and see >:>).
So, i decided to have another look at the unibus boards (i had already
polished the contacts on the boards and the backplane, but anyway...)
and i found out something strange in the installed boards: the M8750
memory module that would be in slot 6 is missing.
Here is a photo of the cardcage panel with the default board dispostion
shown: http://hkzlab.spatof.org/ALBUM/vax-11_725/hpim0261.jpg .

I don't think that the mem module is optional, anyone can confirm this?
and... aonyone got spare modules to sell/give away? :-)
I'd really be happy to get this old system running again!

Bye everyone, and Happy New Year!
