> The ST31230N is at SCSI ID 0, and the error occurs with or without a
> terminator!
> 
>>>> SHOW SCSI
> 
> SCSI = 00000000
>>>> _
> 
> Help me,
> -Vaxima (VAX-Enthusiast since 1983 :-)
> 

Try the console command:

 >>> SET SCSI 7

then check with

 >>> SHOW SCSI

the SCSI adapter ID should be 7 now

When you then issue:

 >>> SHOW DEVICE

You should see the disk at SCSI id 0 and the adapter at SCSI id 7 and 
everything should work like normal now.



